# Shell scripts are line-ending sensitive in a way nothing else here is: a CRLF `install.sh`
# fails on Linux with `bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M`, and in Git Bash on Windows too.
#
# The committed blob is already LF, so this is not fixing anything today -- it is stopping a
# machine with core.autocrlf=true from producing a working copy that cannot run the script it
# just checked out. That is the default on Windows, which is where this repository is developed.
*.sh text eol=lf
